        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0456" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1436: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Nanking (Peck) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-16T16:00:00+08:00">February 16, 1932—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 16—7:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. In view of the probability that disturbance Shanghai-Nanking Railway zone as
                    a result of the present hostilities at Shanghai I have again today advised that
                    American women and children and such men as can be spared evacuate from
                    Chinkiang and Chaotou [?]. Shanghai has already advised all Americans at Soochow
                    and Wusih to evacuate. United States ship <hi rendition="#italic">Bulmer</hi> is
                    at Chinkiang to assist Americans evacuating from or through that port.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
